`HLIT/HDIST/HCLEN` randomized | `inflate_diff.rs::i9_dynamic_literals` | [x] |\n| I10 | `cp_inflate` | `BTYPE=2` dynamic whose code-length stream uses symbols `16`, `17` **and** `18` (all three repeat forms) | `inflate_diff.rs::i10_dynamic_cl_repeats` | [x] |\n| I11 | `cp_inflate` | `BTYPE=2` dynamic with distance symbols `30`/`31` ⇒ `cp_dist_base == 0` ⇒ `backwards_distance == 0` (self-copy loop) | `inflate_diff.rs::i11_dynamic_dist_sym_30_31` | [x] |\n| I12 | `cp_inflate` | `BTYPE=2` dynamic with length symbols `286`/`287` ⇒ `cp_len_base == 0` ⇒ `length == 0` | `inflate_diff.rs::i12_dynamic_len_sym_286_287` | [x] |\n| I13 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block: `BFINAL=0` fixed, `BFINAL=0` fixed, `BFINAL=1` fixed (3 blocks) | `inflate_diff.rs::i13_multi_fixed_blocks` | [x] |\n| I14 | `cp_inflate` | multi-block mixing `BTYPE`: dynamic → fixed → fixed(final), and fixed → dynamic(final) | `inflate_diff.rs::i14_multi_mixed_blocks` | [x] |\n| I15 | `cp_inflate` | dynamic tree with code lengths up to 14 (deep tree, `> 9` ⇒ no `s->lookup` entry) and `HCLEN = 19` / `HCLEN = 4` extremes | `inflate_diff.rs::i15_dynamic_deep_tree` | [x] |\n| I16 | `cp_inflate` | `HLIT` extremes: `nlit = 257` and `nlit = 288`; `HDIST` extremes: `ndst = 1` and `ndst = 32` | `inflate_diff.rs::i16_dynamic_header_extremes` | [x] |\n| I17 | `cp_inflate` | real zlib-format raw deflate (`flate2`, level `0` ⇒ stored) sizes 0…2048 | `inflate_diff.rs::i17_flate2_level0` | [x] |\n| I18 | `cp_inflate` | real raw deflate, levels `1…9`, **random** payloads (literal-heavy) 1…3000 bytes | `inflate_diff.rs::i18_flate2_random` | [x] |\n| I19 | `cp_inflate` | real raw deflate, levels `1…9`, **highly repetitive** payloads (long runs, periodic patterns ⇒ long matches, distance 1) | `inflate_diff.rs::i19_flate2_repetitive` | [x] |\n| I20 | `cp_inflate` | real raw deflate, levels `1…9`, **text-like** payloads (small alphabet, mixed matches) | `inflate_diff.rs::i20_flate2_textlike` | [x] |\n| I21 | `cp_inflate` | input pointer alignment `in & 3 ∈ {0,1,2,3}` (`first_bytes = 0,3,2,1`) × the whole crafted+flate2 corpus | `inflate_diff.rs::i21_input_alignment` | [x] |\n| I22 | `cp_inflate` | `(in_bytes - first_bytes) & 3 ∈ {0,1,2,3}` (`final_word_available`, `count += bits_left`) via trailing padding | `inflate_diff.rs::i22_input_tail_length` | [x] |\n| I23 | `cp_inflate` | `out_bytes` exactly equal to the decompressed size vs. much larger (untouched tail must stay identical) | `inflate_diff.rs::i23_out_bytes_exact_vs_slack` | [x] |\n| I24 | `cp_inflate` | trailing garbage after the final block (extra `in_bytes` that must be ignored) | `inflate_diff.rs::i24_trailing_garbage` | [x] |\n| I25 | `cp_inflate` + globals | `cp_len_base[0]` mutated `3 → 5` before the call ⇒ decoded match length changes; both libraries must change identically | `globals_diff.rs::i25_mutate_len_base` | [x] |\n| I26 | `cp_inflate` + globals | `cp_dist_base[0]` mutated `1 → 2` and `cp_len_extra_bits[8]` `1 → 0` ⇒ different bit consumption | `globals_diff.rs::i26_mutate_dist_base_and_extra_bits` | [x] |\n| I27 | globals | initial contents of all 7 exported data objects read through `dlsym` are byte-identical (and sizes match `nm -S`) | `symbols.rs::exported_globals_have_identical_contents` | [x] |\n| I28 | `cp_inflate` | `cp_fixed_table` mutated to a *different but still valid* canonical length assignment ⇒ `cp_fixed` builds a different tree | `globals_diff.rs::i28_mutate_fixed_table` | [x] |\n| I29 | `cp_inflate` | `cp_permutation_order` rotated within range (still a permutation of 0…18) ⇒ different code-length order | `globals_diff.rs::i29_mutate_permutation_order` | [x] |\n| I30 | `cp_inflate` | fixed block whose literal run crosses every 32-bit word-load boundary (payload lengths 1…64 ⇒ exercises `cp_peak_bits` word vs. final-word paths at every phase) | `inflate_diff.rs::i30_word_boundary_sweep` | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
